  <Section id="tradeoff" title="How many review rounds are worth it" level={3}>
    <Fragment slot="note">From the run records of <a href={issue(204)}>#204</a>, <a href={issue(241)}>#241</a> and <a href={issue(217)}>#217</a>. <a href="#sources">Sources</a>.</Fragment>
    <p>Every review round is another call of the reviewer, and every finding that must be fixed sends the builder back to work. The rounds repeat until one passes, and stop for the owner after five. In the three runs compared here, one round that found nothing took seconds; five rounds that found two real problems took about half of the run.</p>
    <details class="proof">
      <summary>Records: rounds, time and tokens of three runs</summary>
      <Table>
        <caption>Review time: from the start of round 1 to the end of the last review or triage, fixes included. Tokens: the input tokens of every reviewer, triage and fix call, as the providers report them, cached reads included.</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">run</th><th scope="col" class="num">rounds</th><th scope="col">what the rounds found</th><th scope="col">review and fixes</th><th scope="col">active run time</th><th scope="col">tokens of review and fixes</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {costs.map((row) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row"><a href={`#${row.anchor}`}>#{row.issue}</a></th>
              <td data-col="rounds" class="num">{row.rounds}</td>
              <td data-col="what the rounds found">{row.found}</td>
              <td data-col="review and fixes">{row.time}</td>
              <td data-col="active run time">{row.run}</td>
              <td data-col="tokens of review and fixes">{row.tokens}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </Table>
      <p>What the extra rounds bought: in #217, round 3 found that the fix of round 1 could still let a raised finding lose its severity, which would have weakened the very check the Issue was written to protect. Round 2, which read only the fix, found nothing; the gap showed when round 3 read the complete feature again. What they cost: the review and its two fixes took 46 of the 90 minutes, and about twelve times the tokens of the single round of #204. In #241 the one finding cost under three minutes. A round that finds nothing, as in #204, costs seconds.</p>
    </details>
